From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nougat: loudspeaker COD, SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN 1024, partial-attr
 heap fix

Three fixes so phones treat U2 as an audio sink and complete SDP discovery:

1. BTA_DM_COD {0x5A,0x02,0x0C} (phone/smartphone) -> {0x24,0x04,0x14}
   (Audio/Video, Loudspeaker; service bits Audio|Rendering).  With the phone
   COD, sources classify U2 as a peer phone after pairing (icon downgrades to
   generic bluetooth, no media-audio offer).

2. SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN 400 -> 1024.  Our registered records contain a 662-byte
   attribute; sdp_server truncates via sdpu_build_partial_attrib_entry(),
   which logs "len 662 exceeds SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN" and clamps to 400, corrupting
   the continuation state -- the phone receives an incomplete attribute list,
   finds no AudioSink UUID and refuses A2DP.

3. sdpu_build_partial_attrib_entry() allocated a fixed SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN
   buffer but built the full attribute into it -- heap overflow for any
   attribute larger than the cap.  Allocate attr_len instead (mirrors the
   upstream AOSP fix).
---
diff --git a/include/bt_target.h b/include/bt_target.h
--- a/include/bt_target.h
+++ b/include/bt_target.h
@@ -388,13 +388,16 @@
 /* Default class of device
 * {SERVICE_CLASS, MAJOR_CLASS, MINOR_CLASS}
 *
-* SERVICE_CLASS:0x5A (Bit17 -Networking,Bit19 - Capturing,Bit20 -Object Transfer,Bit22 -Telephony)
-* MAJOR_CLASS:0x02 - PHONE
-* MINOR_CLASS:0x0C - SMART_PHONE
+* SERVICE_CLASS:0x24 (Bit21 -Audio,Bit18 -Rendering)
+* MAJOR_CLASS:0x04 - AUDIO_VIDEO
+* MINOR_CLASS:0x14 - LOUDSPEAKER
 *
+* U2 is a Bluetooth audio RECEIVER (A2DP sink): advertising the phone COD
+* (0x5A020C) makes source devices classify it as a peer phone (file transfer)
+* and never offer media audio.  Loudspeaker COD makes phones auto-offer A2DP.
 */
 #ifndef BTA_DM_COD
-#define BTA_DM_COD {0x5A, 0x02, 0x0C}
+#define BTA_DM_COD {0x24, 0x04, 0x14}
 #endif
 
 /* The number of SCO links. */
@@ -852,7 +855,7 @@
 
 /* The maximum length, in bytes, of an attribute. */
 #ifndef SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN
-#define SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN            400
+#define SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN            1024
 #endif
 
 /* The maximum number of attribute filters supported by SDP databases. */
diff --git a/stack/sdp/sdp_utils.c b/stack/sdp/sdp_utils.c
--- a/stack/sdp/sdp_utils.c
+++ b/stack/sdp/sdp_utils.c
@@ -1020,11 +1020,13 @@
 *******************************************************************************/
 UINT8 *sdpu_build_partial_attrib_entry (UINT8 *p_out, tSDP_ATTRIBUTE *p_attr, UINT16 len, UINT16 *offset)
 {
-    UINT8 *p_attr_buff = (UINT8 *)osi_malloc(sizeof(UINT8) * SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN);
-    sdpu_build_attrib_entry(p_attr_buff, p_attr);
-
     UINT16 attr_len = sdpu_get_attrib_entry_len(p_attr);
 
+    /* Allocate for the real attribute length: building into a fixed
+     * SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN buffer overflows the heap for larger attributes. */
+    UINT8 *p_attr_buff = (UINT8 *)osi_malloc(sizeof(UINT8) * attr_len);
+    sdpu_build_attrib_entry(p_attr_buff, p_attr);
+
     if (len > SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN)
     {
         SDP_TRACE_ERROR("%s len %d exceeds SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN", __func__, len);
-- 
